   "source": [
    "### Orchestration — interactive, per-change confirmation\n",
    "\n",
    "**Nothing is applied automatically** (unless `HEADLESS=True`, Section 1 — then\n",
    "every rule is auto-applied to every patent so the notebook can run\n",
    "unattended). The `RuleReviewPipeline` below walks the rules one at a time,\n",
    "in order (see `PIPELINE_RULES`):\n",
    "\n",
    "0. Ghost-block cleanup → **TR. `topType` TP→TR codebook rename (all batches)**\n",
    "→ A. Combined-Thrust flag → C. `UAVSimilar` propagation (D3-excluded, Bug-2\n",
    "fix) → D. duplicate inheritance → A1. fixed-arch `acState`→`HoverCruise`\n",
    "auto-set (Bug-1 fix pt.1) → E. `acState` Ground→Other, convertible-arch only\n",
    "(Bug-1 fix pt.2) → New. multi-architecture `aircraftName_perArch` suffix\n",
    "(Part C) → BC. `boom<N>_count` True/False → 1/0.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Removed 2026-08-23.** Step 0b (`empKin`→`empTilts`), Step 0c (Draft→`acSty`),\n",
    "Rule B and its retroactive check, Rule F and Rule H (`boomXFormat`), Rule G\n",
    "(`fusKin` \"Variable\") and **A3** (TB→`fusKin=TiltBody`) are gone from this\n",
    "notebook. The first six only ever fired on a pre-v15_3 export, and those\n",
    "batches now go through `02a_legacy.ipynb`, whose wizard round-trip performs\n",
    "the same migrations using the wizard's own code — keeping a second\n",
    "implementation here would mean two things that have to agree with no test that\n",
    "they do. **A3 was deleted rather than moved:** it force-overwrote `fusKin` on\n",
    "every TB patent, and under the current codebook `LevelCabin` is a legitimate\n",
    "answer for a TB, so A3 would erase exactly the answers the review queue exists\n",
    "to collect. Do not reintroduce anything with that behaviour.\n",
    "\n",
    "For each rule it does a **dry run** and explains itself in plain language\n",
    "before showing anything: a *What this rule does* paragraph, and a box saying\n",
    "what **✔ APPLY** and **✘ SKIP** each mean **for that specific rule** (the\n",
    "per-rule wording lives in `_RULE_HELP` — add an entry there when you add a\n",
    "rule). Then it shows every patent the rule would touch, with its figure and a\n",
    "readable diff as bullets (`Change <field>: old → new`, `Add …`, `Delete …`,\n",
    "plus the audit-trail note), and one green/grey button per patent (all set to\n",
    "**APPLY** by default):\n",
    "\n",
    "- **✔ APPLY** (green, default) — let the rule change this patent.\n",
    "- **✘ SKIP** (grey) — leave this patent exactly as the labeller left it.\n",
    "- **Apply ticked → next rule** — writes the change for the APPLY patents only;\n",
    "  SKIP patents keep their current rows untouched. Also at the bottom of the page.\n",
    "- **Skip this rule (change nothing)** — nothing applied for any patent, move on.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The list is paged** — only a handful of patents are shown at a time so the\n",
    "figures can be big enough to judge:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **◀ Prev / Next ▶ / Go to page** move between groups. Ticks are kept for\n",
    "  every patent of the rule, on every page, until you press *Apply ticked* —\n",
    "  paging never resets them.\n",
    "- **Per page** (default 4) and **Image size** (default 520 px) are dropdowns in\n",
    "  the paging bar; other defaults can be set at construction:\n",
    "  `RuleReviewPipeline(df, page_size=6, img_px=720)`.\n",
    "- **✔/✘ this page** ticks or unticks only what's on screen; **✔/✘ ALL patents**\n",
    "  covers every page of the current rule. The live counter above the list always\n",
    "  says how many patents will be changed vs left untouched.\n",
    "- Figures are only loaded for the page you're looking at, so a rule touching\n",
    "  hundreds of patents renders immediately.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Rows that start on ✘ SKIP.** A rule can mark a patent as *suspicious input*\n",
    "via `_row_caution()`; those rows open on **SKIP** with an amber banner saying\n",
    "why, and the header counts them. Nothing happens to them unless you switch\n",
    "them to APPLY yourself. Today only **A1** does this: a rigid architecture looks\n",
    "the same in hover and in cruise, so if a patent's figures were given *different*\n",
    "flight states, either the architecture label or the states are wrong — forcing\n",
    "everything to HoverCruise would bury that. 9 of the 31 A1 patents in Batch_01\n",
    "trip it (e.g. `US2019144126A1` and `US2017203839A1`, both labelled `MR` but\n",
    "drawn with a wing, a tail and tilting ducts). The fix for those is `topType` in\n",
    "the wizard, not `acState` here.\n",
    "\n",
    "Ghost-block cleanup (step 0) is the one that needs the most explaining, so it\n",
    "renders its own **old-vs-kept comparison table**: the same image file was\n",
    "answered twice (an abandoned half-filled attempt and the finished review), and\n",
    "the row shows field by field which answers die and which survive untouched. If\n",
    "*no* entry for that image would survive, the row says so in red — that would be\n",
    "real data loss, not a ghost.\n",
    "\n",
    "The pipeline works on its own copy — your `df` is only updated when you run\n",
    "the `df = pipeline.result()` cell after finishing. The completeness check\n",
    "(report-only, changes nothing) runs inside that same cell.\n",
    "\n",
    "Rule A is still flag-only here: applying it just marks the patent for the\n",
    "Section 5 review queue, where you make the actual call with the drawing in\n",
    "front of you. A4 (assert zero `duplicateType == '4'`) runs earlier,\n",
    "in Section 3, right after loading — before any of the rules above, since a\n",
    "nonzero count stops the notebook outright rather than flowing through the\n",
    "pipeline."
   ]
  },
