   "source": [
    "### Unanswered-question check — asks the WIZARD, not the spreadsheet\n",
    "\n",
    "The completeness check above finds rows that EXIST with a blank value. A question the\n",
    "reviewer never answered has no row at all, so it is invisible to it — and knowing which\n",
    "questions *should* have been asked means knowing the wizard's conditional logic (winged\n",
    "vs wingless card sets, `isOtherArch` turning M1–M3 into free text, `wCount` driving the\n",
    "wing blocks, `quickOverride` hiding the structured count, …).\n",
    "\n",
    "Re-implementing that in Python would leave two copies to drift apart. So this runs each\n",
    "patent through the real wizard in Node and calls **`nextBlockers()`** — the same function\n",
    "that gates the Next button in the UI. One source of truth. Report-only: it changes\n",
    "nothing, and writes a worklist CSV beside the other proposals."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9c5a64ed",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "asking the wizard (UI_for_taxonomy_caracterization_15_4.html) what 124 patent(s) are still missing — one Node process each, this takes a minute…\n",
